-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 2, §2.1 כללי
-- Kindergarten teachers in general: the unit of work and the kindergarten's
-- hours, an additional month of study, the supplement equal to three
-- education hours, substitution for an absent teacher or assistant and its
-- payments, holiday-eve celebrations, the transfer agreements of 1981, the
-- mother kindergarten teacher, and pointers to the rules shared with
-- elementary-school teachers.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `2.1 כללי`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p2 The page's table of contents ("contents of the page").
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p3 Table of contents: 2.1.1.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p4 Table of contents: 2.1.2.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p5 Table of contents: 2.1.3.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p6 Table of contents: 2.1.4.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p7 Table of contents: 2.1.5.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p8 Table of contents: 2.1.8.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p9 Table of contents: 2.1.9.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p10 Table of contents: 2.1.10.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p11 Table of contents: 2.1.12.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1/p12 Table of contents: age hours.

-- The parties of the kindergarten. The teacher, the owner, the supervisor and
-- the district come from common; the assistant, the person in charge in the
-- district (א(1)) and the person an owner names to handle substitutions are
-- this section's own.
DECLARE `2.1 party` IS ONE OF
    `a takanon party` HAS `who` IS A Party
    `the kindergarten assistant`
    `the person in charge in the district`
    `the person responsible for substitutions`

DECLARE `kindergarten action` IS ONE OF
    `notify of own absence`                         HAS `notified` IS A LIST OF `2.1 party`
    `notify in advance of a long absence`           HAS `notified in advance` IS A LIST OF `2.1 party`
    `do her best to notify the authority or owner of the teacher's absence`
    `ask the assistant to watch the children`
    `notify of the assistant's absence`
    `send a substitute`                             HAS `substitute` IS A `kind of substitute`
    `exhaust every option to send a substitute`
    `arrange a substitute for the assistant`
    `name a person responsible for substitutions and a deputy`
    `name a person to turn to when an assistant is absent`
    `prepare lists of candidates to substitute for teachers`
    `prepare an additional candidate list, consulting the kindergarten supervisor`
    `prepare lists of candidates to substitute for assistants`
    `supervise the children until relieved`
    `claim the payment for being alone`             HAS `claim details complete` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pay the assistant's daily compensation`        HAS `compensation` IS A NUMBER
    `set parents' reception times`                  HAS `some outside the kindergarten's regular hours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hold the year's parents' meetings`             HAS `meetings held` IS A NUMBER
    `visit the child's home`
    `pay the education-hours supplement`            HAS `supplement paid` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `kind of substitute` IS ONE OF
    `an unplaced kindergarten teacher`
    `an unplaced teacher`
    `a kindergarten teacher from an accelerated course`
    `a kindergarten-teachers' seminar student`
    `a twelfth-grade graduate after a colloquium`
    `a candidate from the additional list`

§§ `2.1.1 Unit of work`

-- 1: in 5752 and 5753 kindergartens open six days a week, Sunday to Thursday
-- 07:55-13:20 and Friday 07:55-12:45; the teachers work five days. Times are
-- minutes from midnight; a school year is named by the Gregorian year it
-- begins in (5752 = 1991, 5753 = 1992).
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_1__para_1
GIVEN `school year beginning in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the six-day week of 2.1.1.1 holds in` `school year beginning in` IF
    `school year beginning in` EQUALS 1991 OR `school year beginning in` EQUALS 1992

DECLARE `weekday` IS ONE OF Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday

GIVEN d IS A `weekday`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minutes the kindergarten is open` d IS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN Friday   THEN (12 TIMES 60 PLUS 45) MINUS (7 TIMES 60 PLUS 55)
    WHEN Saturday THEN 0
    OTHERWISE          (13 TIMES 60 PLUS 20) MINUS (7 TIMES 60 PLUS 55)

`days a kindergarten teacher works` MEANS 5

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_1__para_2
`weekly teaching hours in a unit` MEANS 27
`weekly education hours in a unit` MEANS 3
`weekly hours in a kindergarten teacher's unit` MEANS `weekly teaching hours in a unit` PLUS `weekly education hours in a unit`

-- 3: a complementing kindergarten teacher works by weekly hours, is paid by
-- grade and seniority, and her weekly day is worth 5/28 of a position,
-- subject to age hours and the mother supplement.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_1__para_3
GIVEN `days a week` IS A NUMBER, `adjustment for age hours and mother supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `position fraction of a complementing teacher` `days a week` `adjustment for age hours and mother supplement` IS
    `days a week` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 28 TIMES `adjustment for age hours and mother supplement`

-- 5/28 is, to four places, the Friday morning (12:45 less 07:55) as a share
-- of the five Sunday-to-Thursday mornings a full-time teacher works — the
-- sixth day a complementing teacher covers. The text does not say so; the
-- check is that the figure is consistent with the hours of 1.
`5/28 is the Friday morning as a share of five weekday mornings` MEANS
    TRUNC (`minutes the kindergarten is open` Friday DIVIDED BY (5 TIMES `minutes the kindergarten is open` Sunday)) 3
        EQUALS TRUNC (5 DIVIDED BY 28) 3
#ASSERT `5/28 is the Friday morning as a share of five weekday mornings`

-- 4: where complementing teachers are lacking, teachers may work extra and
-- the sixth day's hours are excess hours.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_1__para_4
GIVEN `complementing teachers are lacking` IS A BOOLEAN, `sixth-day hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `excess hours from the sixth day` `complementing teachers are lacking` `sixth-day hours` IS
    IF `complementing teachers are lacking` THEN `sixth-day hours` ELSE 0

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_1/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_1/p2 A source: agreement with the Teachers' Union of 15.7.91.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_1/p3 A source: special director-general's circular, copy 24, of 21.7.85.

§§ `2.1.2 An additional month of study`

DECLARE `additional month` HAS
    `prior approval of the district office`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the permanent teacher continues`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `another teacher approved by the supervision`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `two training-institution students with the institution's consent, under guidance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `physical conditions checked by the supervisor`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `feeding continues`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the teacher takes part in training for it`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `budget for work materials provided`                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2/p1 akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2/p2
GIVEN m IS AN `additional month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the additional month may open` m IF
        m's `prior approval of the district office`
    AND `staffed under 2.1.2.1` m
    AND `condition 2: physical conditions` m
    AND `condition 3: feeding` m
    AND `condition 4: training` m
    AND `condition 5: materials budget` m

-- 1: it is preferable (רצוי) that the permanent teacher continue; another
-- teacher needs the supervision's approval; ¶2: instead of a teacher, two
-- students of a kindergarten-teacher training institution, with its
-- management's consent and under guidance.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2__para_1 akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2__para_1/p2
GIVEN m IS AN `additional month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `staffed under 2.1.2.1` m IF
        m's `the permanent teacher continues`
    OR  m's `another teacher approved by the supervision`
    OR  m's `two training-institution students with the institution's consent, under guidance`

GIVEN m IS AN `additional month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `staffed as 2.1.2.1 prefers` m IF
    m's `the permanent teacher continues`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2__para_2
GIVEN m IS AN `additional month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 2: physical conditions` m IF m's `physical conditions checked by the supervisor`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2__para_3
GIVEN m IS AN `additional month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 3: feeding` m IF m's `feeding continues`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2__para_4
GIVEN m IS AN `additional month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 4: training` m IF m's `the teacher takes part in training for it`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2__para_5
GIVEN m IS AN `additional month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 5: materials budget` m IF m's `budget for work materials provided`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2/p3 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_2/p4 A source: director-general's circular לד/10, section 228.

§§ `2.1.3 The supplement equal to three education hours`

-- 1: besides the administrative responsibility for running the kindergarten,
-- the teacher bears pedagogical responsibility for the children's education.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3__para_1
`a kindergarten teacher bears pedagogical responsibility` MEANS TRUE

-- 1 ¶2: at the start of the year she sets times to receive parents, also
-- outside the kindergarten's regular hours, convenes at least two parents'
-- meetings during the year, and visits the parents' homes when needed; so
-- she gets a supplement equal to the pay of 3 weekly hours, by her education
-- and recognised seniority. Time in school months from the start of the year
-- ("the start of the year" is read as its first month).
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3__para_1/p2
GIVEN `a home visit is needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `the parents' duties of 2.1.3` `a home visit is needed` IS
    (PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
     MUST  `set parents' reception times` outside PROVIDED outside
     WITHIN 1
     LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "2.1.3.1: parents' reception times, also outside regular hours, are set at the start of the year")
    RAND
    (PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
     MUST  `hold the year's parents' meetings` n PROVIDED n AT LEAST 2
     WITHIN 12
     LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "2.1.3.1: at least two parents' meetings during the year")
    RAND
    (IF `a home visit is needed`
     THEN PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
          MUST  `visit the child's home`
          LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "2.1.3.1: she visits the parents' homes when needed"
     ELSE FULFILLED)

GIVEN `pay of one weekly hour, by education and recognised seniority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `education-hours supplement` `pay of one weekly hour, by education and recognised seniority` IS
    3 TIMES `pay of one weekly hour, by education and recognised seniority`

-- 2: paid every month of the year, all twelve.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3__para_2
GIVEN `pay of one weekly hour, by education and recognised seniority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `the supplement every month` `pay of one weekly hour, by education and recognised seniority` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the education-hours supplement` s
          PROVIDED s AT LEAST `education-hours supplement` `pay of one weekly hour, by education and recognised seniority`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the employer` BECAUSE "2.1.3.2: the supplement is paid every month of the year"

`months a year the supplement is paid` MEANS 12

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3__para_3
GIVEN p IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may supervise a kindergarten teacher's work` p IF
    p EQUALS `the supervisor`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3/p2 A source: special collective agreement of 16.11.83; director-general's circular מד/5.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3/p3 A source: special director-general's circulars of 5734 and 5737.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3/p4 A source: director-general's circular לה/4, section 91, and the conditions-of-service head's clarification.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_3/p5 A source: director-general's circular לה/4, section 91.

§§ `2.1.4-2.1.5 Probation, tenure and dismissal`

-- The rules for an elementary-school teacher apply. They are sections 3.4
-- and 3.5, named inputs here.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_4/p1
ASSUME `the probation and tenure rules of section 3.4` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO BOOLEAN

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_4/p2 A pointer to section 3.4.

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_5/p1
ASSUME `the dismissal rules of section 3.5` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO BOOLEAN

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_5/p2 A pointer to section 3.5.

§§ `2.1.8 Substitution`

-- ¶1: every kindergarten class has two workers, a teacher and an assistant,
-- from 8:00 to 12:30.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p1
GIVEN `teachers present` IS A NUMBER, `assistants present` IS A NUMBER, `minute of the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the class is properly staffed` `teachers present` `assistants present` `minute of the day` IF
        (NOT (`minute of the day` AT LEAST 8 TIMES 60 AND `minute of the day` AT MOST 12 TIMES 60 PLUS 30))
    OR  (`teachers present` AT LEAST 1 AND `assistants present` AT LEAST 1)

-- ¶2: when one of the two is absent, a substitute is arranged the same day,
-- by the guidelines below: for the teacher by the person responsible for
-- substitutions (א(3), א(5)), for the assistant by the owner (ב(1)). Time in
-- minutes from the moment the absence is known.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p2
DECLARE `absent worker` IS ONE OF `the kindergarten teacher`, `the assistant`

GIVEN w IS AN `absent worker`, `minutes left in the working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `a substitute the same day` w `minutes left in the working day` IS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `the kindergarten teacher` THEN
        PARTY `the person responsible for substitutions`
        MUST  `send a substitute` s
        WITHIN `minutes left in the working day`
        LEST  BREACH BY `the person responsible for substitutions` BECAUSE "2.1.8: a substitute for the teacher is arranged the same day"
    WHEN `the assistant` THEN
        PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
        MUST  `arrange a substitute for the assistant`
        WITHIN `minutes left in the working day`
        LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8: a substitute for the assistant is arranged the same day"

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p3 A heading ("א. substituting for an absent kindergarten teacher").
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p4 A heading ("(1) the teacher's notice of her absence").

-- א(1): a teacher who finds she cannot come notifies at once, herself or by
-- a messenger. In the big cities she reports at once to the person in charge
-- in the district and to the owner. Elsewhere the clause names no addressee;
-- א(3) names the person to be turned to when a teacher is absent, and she is
-- read as the one. Where the absence may pass ten days, she also notifies
-- the supervisor and the owner in advance. "At once" carries no number; it
-- is an input.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p5
GIVEN `in a big city` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `2.1 party`
DECIDE `whom the absent teacher notifies at once` `in a big city` IS
    IF `in a big city`
    THEN LIST `the person in charge in the district`, `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
    ELSE LIST `the person responsible for substitutions`

`whom she notifies in advance of an absence that may pass ten days` MEANS
    LIST `a takanon party` `the supervisor`, `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`

GIVEN `in a big city` IS A BOOLEAN, `may exceed ten days` IS A BOOLEAN, `minutes that count as at once` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `the teacher's notice` `in a big city` `may exceed ten days` `minutes that count as at once` IS
    (PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
     MUST  `notify of own absence` whom
           PROVIDED all (GIVEN w YIELD elem w whom) (`whom the absent teacher notifies at once` `in a big city`)
     WITHIN `minutes that count as at once`
     LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(1): the absent teacher notifies at once")
    RAND
    (IF `may exceed ten days`
     THEN PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
          MUST  `notify in advance of a long absence` whom
                PROVIDED all (GIVEN w YIELD elem w whom) `whom she notifies in advance of an absence that may pass ten days`
          LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(1): an absence that may pass ten days is notified in advance to the supervisor and the owner"
     ELSE FULFILLED)

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p6 A heading ("(2) the assistant's notice of the teacher's absence").

-- א(2): if neither the permanent teacher nor a substitute has come by 8:30,
-- the assistant does her best to notify the authority or owner, by phone or
-- messenger; the person responsible for substitutions asks her to watch the
-- children until the earliest of the end of the day, the teacher's arrival
-- and the substitute's.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p7
GIVEN `teacher or substitute present at 8:30` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `the assistant's notice` `teacher or substitute present at 8:30` IS
    IF `teacher or substitute present at 8:30`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the kindergarten assistant`
         MUST  `do her best to notify the authority or owner of the teacher's absence`
         HENCE (PARTY `the person responsible for substitutions`
                MUST  `ask the assistant to watch the children`
                HENCE (PARTY `the kindergarten assistant`
                       MUST  `supervise the children until relieved`)
                LEST  BREACH BY `the person responsible for substitutions` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(2): the responsible person asks the assistant to watch the children")
         LEST  BREACH BY `the kindergarten assistant` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(2): the assistant notifies of the teacher's absence"

GIVEN `end of the working day` IS A NUMBER, `teacher arrives` IS A NUMBER, `substitute arrives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the assistant watches the children until` `end of the working day` `teacher arrives` `substitute arrives` IS
    minimum (LIST `end of the working day`, `teacher arrives`, `substitute arrives`)

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p8 A heading ("(3) naming a person responsible for substitutions").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p9
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `naming a responsible person` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `name a person responsible for substitutions and a deputy`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(3): every owner names a person responsible for substitutions, and a deputy"

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p10 A heading ("(4) preparing a list of substitute candidates").

-- א(4): the owners of the kindergarten teachers (district offices, local
-- authorities, organisations) prepare lists of suitable candidates, in this
-- order of priority. The additional list (¶17, א(5)) comes after all five.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p11
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `the owners' candidate lists` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `prepare lists of candidates to substitute for teachers`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(4): the owners prepare lists of candidates to substitute for absent teachers"

GIVEN s IS A `kind of substitute`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `priority of the candidate` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `a candidate from the additional list` THEN 6
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p12
    WHEN `an unplaced kindergarten teacher` THEN 1
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p13
    WHEN `an unplaced teacher` THEN 2
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p14
    WHEN `a kindergarten teacher from an accelerated course` THEN 3
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p15
    WHEN `a kindergarten-teachers' seminar student` THEN 4
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p16
    WHEN `a twelfth-grade graduate after a colloquium` THEN 5

-- ¶17: where an additional list is needed, it is prepared in consultation
-- with the kindergarten supervisor; separate lists for state and
-- state-religious kindergartens; all prepared at the start of the school
-- year, by every owner and local authority (school month 1).
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p17
DECLARE `stream` IS ONE OF `state`, `state-religious`

GIVEN `an additional list is needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `lists at the start of the year` `an additional list is needed` IS
    (PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
     MUST  `prepare lists of candidates to substitute for teachers`
     WITHIN 1
     LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(4): the candidate lists are prepared at the start of the school year")
    RAND
    (IF `an additional list is needed`
     THEN PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
          MUST  `prepare an additional candidate list, consulting the kindergarten supervisor`
          WITHIN 1
          LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(4): an additional list is prepared in consultation with the kindergarten supervisor"
     ELSE FULFILLED)

GIVEN `kindergarten's stream` IS A `stream`, `candidate's list` IS A `stream`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate's list fits the kindergarten` `kindergarten's stream` `candidate's list` IF
    `kindergarten's stream` EQUALS `candidate's list`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p18 A heading ("(5) sending a substitute to the kindergarten").

-- א(5): the responsible person sends a substitute at once, by the order of
-- priority; the additional list only if none of (א)-(ה) is available. In a
-- double kindergarten the teacher present watches both classes, with both
-- assistants; in a single class the assistant watches until the substitute
-- comes.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p19
GIVEN available IS A LIST OF `kind of substitute`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `sending by priority` available IS
    PARTY `the person responsible for substitutions`
    MUST  `send a substitute` s
          PROVIDED all (GIVEN a YIELD `priority of the candidate` s AT MOST `priority of the candidate` a) available
    LEST  BREACH BY `the person responsible for substitutions` BECAUSE "2.1.8 א(5): the substitute is sent from the list by priority"

DECLARE `who watches the children` IS ONE OF
    `the other teacher of the double kindergarten, with both assistants`
    `the assistant, until the substitute comes`

GIVEN `a double kindergarten` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `who watches the children`
DECIDE `who watches until the substitute comes` `a double kindergarten` IS
    IF `a double kindergarten`
    THEN `the other teacher of the double kindergarten, with both assistants`
    ELSE `the assistant, until the substitute comes`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p20 A heading ("ב. substituting for an absent assistant").
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p21 A heading ("(1) the assistant's notice of her absence").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p22
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `the absent assistant` IS
    (PARTY `the kindergarten assistant`
     MUST  `notify of own absence` whom
           PROVIDED elem (`a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`) whom
                AND elem (`a takanon party` `the teaching employee`) whom
     LEST  BREACH BY `the kindergarten assistant` BECAUSE "2.1.8 ב(1): the absent assistant notifies the owner and the teacher at once")
    RAND
    (PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
     MUST  `arrange a substitute for the assistant`
     LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 ב(1): the owner arranges a substitute for the assistant")

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p23 A heading ("(2) the teacher's notice of the assistant's absence").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p24
GIVEN `assistant present at 8:30` IS A BOOLEAN, `told a substitute is coming` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `the teacher's notice of the assistant's absence` `assistant present at 8:30` `told a substitute is coming` IS
    IF `assistant present at 8:30` OR `told a substitute is coming`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `notify of the assistant's absence`
         LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "2.1.8 ב(2): the teacher reports the assistant's absence"

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p25 A heading ("(3) the qualifications of an assistant's substitute").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p26
DECLARE `assistant's substitute` HAS
    `age`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `clean and tidy appearance`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `inclined to work with children`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `responsible at work`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `elementary knowledge of child care`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `reads and writes Hebrew at elementary-school level` IS A BOOLEAN
    `can keep an orderly household`          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS AN `assistant's substitute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualified to substitute for an assistant` c IF
        c's `age` AT LEAST 18
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p27
    AND c's `clean and tidy appearance`
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p28
    AND c's `inclined to work with children`
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p29
    AND c's `responsible at work`
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p30
    AND c's `elementary knowledge of child care`
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p31
    AND c's `reads and writes Hebrew at elementary-school level`
    @ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p32
    AND c's `can keep an orderly household`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p33 A heading ("(4) naming a person responsible for substitutions").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p34
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `naming a responsible person for assistants` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `name a person to turn to when an assistant is absent`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 ב(4): every owner employing assistants names a person to turn to when one is absent"

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p35 A heading ("(5) list of substitute candidates").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p36
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `lists of assistants' substitutes` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `prepare lists of candidates to substitute for assistants`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 ב(5): the owners prepare lists of substitutes for assistants"

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p37 A heading ("ג. arrangements in small localities").

-- ג: in small localities the owners run special arrangements, under the
-- district office's guidance and supervision. What they are is left to them.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p38
GIVEN `a small locality` IS A BOOLEAN, `special arrangement under the district's guidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `substitution in a small locality is arranged` `a small locality` `special arrangement under the district's guidance` IF
    (NOT `a small locality`) OR `special arrangement under the district's guidance`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p39 A heading ("ד. payments").
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p40 A heading ("(1) payments to the teacher and a permanent assistant").

-- ד(1) ¶41: in the teacher's absence and with no substitute, every option to
-- send a substitute is exhausted.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p41
GIVEN `the teacher is absent and no substitute has come` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `every option is exhausted first` `the teacher is absent and no substitute has come` IS
    IF `the teacher is absent and no substitute has come`
    THEN PARTY `the person responsible for substitutions`
         MUST  `exhaust every option to send a substitute`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the person responsible for substitutions` BECAUSE "2.1.8 ד(1): every option to send a substitute is exhausted"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ד(1): an assistant alone in her class gets, from the owner, a global sum
-- for each working day, bearing no other benefits, on top of her salary, if
-- she works at least two hours beyond her regular hours that day. The sum
-- is not given here: an input.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p42
GIVEN `alone in the class` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours beyond her regular hours` IS A NUMBER, `the global daily sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `daily compensation for being alone` `alone in the class` `hours beyond her regular hours` `the global daily sum` IS
    IF `alone in the class` AND `hours beyond her regular hours` AT LEAST 2
    THEN `the global daily sum`
    ELSE 0

-- ¶43: paid by the teacher's owner from the first day of the absence; the
-- assistant claims it from the owner, giving dates, place and institution.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p43
GIVEN `compensation due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2.1 party` `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `claiming the compensation` `compensation due` IS
    PARTY `the kindergarten assistant`
    MAY   `claim the payment for being alone` complete PROVIDED complete
    HENCE (PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body`
           MUST  `pay the assistant's daily compensation` c PROVIDED c AT LEAST `compensation due`
           LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "2.1.8 ד(1): the owner pays the assistant's compensation from the first day")

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p44 A heading ("(2) payment to a kindergarten teacher's substitute").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p45
GIVEN `combined monthly salary of a senior kindergarten teacher in her third year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hourly pay of a teacher's substitute` `combined monthly salary of a senior kindergarten teacher in her third year` IS
    (`combined monthly salary of a senior kindergarten teacher in her third year` DIVIDED BY 120) TIMES 1.2

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p46 A heading ("(3) payment to an assistant's substitute").

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p47
GIVEN `the assistants' pay rates for the work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay of an assistant's substitute` `the assistants' pay rates for the work` IS
    `the assistants' pay rates for the work`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p48 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p49 A source: director-general's circular לד/7, section 132.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p50 A source: director-general's circular לו/6; planning and budget division circular of 12.10.81.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p51 A source: director-general's circulars לח/6 and שן/3; collective agreement of 15.5.91.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_8/p52 A source: director-general's circular לד/8, section 182.

§§ `2.1.9 Holiday eves in the kindergarten`

-- ¶1: involving parents in the kindergarten's celebrations is recommended
-- through the year: a permission the teacher may use, no duty.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_9/p1
`involving parents in celebrations is recommended, not required` MEANS TRUE

-- ¶2: three times a year (Hanukkah, Purim, the end of the year) a teacher who
-- celebrates with parents in the afternoon — and only she — may end the day
-- at 11:00; a Purim morning celebration in costume ends at 11:30.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_9/p2
DECLARE `celebration` IS ONE OF Hanukkah, Purim, `end of the school year`, `other occasion`

GIVEN c IS A `celebration`, `with parents in the afternoon` IS A BOOLEAN, `a costumed Purim morning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `earliest end of the day` c `with parents in the afternoon` `a costumed Purim morning` IS
    IF c EQUALS Purim AND `a costumed Purim morning`
    THEN JUST (11 TIMES 60 PLUS 30)
    ELSE IF (NOT c EQUALS `other occasion`) AND `with parents in the afternoon`
         THEN JUST (11 TIMES 60)
         ELSE NOTHING

-- ¶3: celebrations with parents need their consent; dates are agreed at a
-- parents' meeting by the majority of those present, or with an elected
-- parents' committee.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_9/p3
GIVEN `in favour at the parents' meeting` IS A NUMBER, `present` IS A NUMBER, `agreed with the elected committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the celebration's date is agreed` `in favour at the parents' meeting` `present` `agreed with the elected committee` IF
    `in favour at the parents' meeting` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `present` OR `agreed with the elected committee`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_9/p4 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_9/p5 A source: director-general's circular שם/1, section 43.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_9/p6 A source: director-general's circulars שם/5 and מא/5.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_9/p7 A source: director-general's circular מח/2, section 92.

§§ `2.1.10 The transfer of kindergarten teachers to the State service`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_1/p1 An introduction to the agreements of 27.9.1981; their text is a linked document, not part of this section's text.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_1/p2 The title of the special collective agreement, linked, not reproduced.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_1/p3 The agreement's full title and date (27.9.1981); its terms are in the linked document.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_1/p4 The title of the agreement's annex, linked, not reproduced.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_1/p5 The title of the transfer form under section 4.2 of the agreement, linked, not reproduced.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_1/p6 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_1/p7 A source: director-general's circular מב/4, sections 133-134.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_2/p1 The title of the special collective agreement on severance pay, linked, not reproduced.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_10_2/p2 The agreement's full title and date (27.9.1981); its terms are in the linked document.

§§ `2.1.12 The mother kindergarten teacher`

DECLARE `mother kindergarten teacher` HAS
    `position fraction`                     IS A NUMBER
    `substitute approved by the supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a coordinating teacher required by her employer to work a full position` IS A BOOLEAN
    `mother of a child up to 14`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to age hours`                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- 1: a mother teacher in a full position may be absent up to 3 weekly hours
-- if a substitute approved by the supervision is found.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12__para_1
GIVEN m IS A `mother kindergarten teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly hours she may be absent` m IS
    IF m's `position fraction` AT LEAST 1 AND m's `substitute approved by the supervision`
    THEN 3
    ELSE 0

-- 2: her salary is computed as a mother teacher's (section 1.13), a named
-- input. ¶2's note: one day's absence every two weeks — working 90% and paid
-- for 100%; or no absence — working 100% and paid for 110%.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12__para_2
ASSUME `the mother-teacher salary of section 1.13` IS A FUNCTION FROM `mother kindergarten teacher` TO NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12__para_2/p2
GIVEN `takes a day off every two weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of a position worked` `takes a day off every two weeks` IS
    IF `takes a day off every two weeks` THEN 0.9 ELSE 1

GIVEN `takes a day off every two weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of a position paid` `takes a day off every two weeks` IS
    IF `takes a day off every two weeks` THEN 1 ELSE 1.1

-- The note's arithmetic agrees with 1 and with 2.1.1: one day in two weeks
-- is half a day a week, three of the unit's thirty hours, 10%.
`a day in two weeks is 10% of the unit` MEANS
    `weekly hours in a kindergarten teacher's unit` DIVIDED BY `days a kindergarten teacher works` DIVIDED BY 2
        EQUALS `weekly hours in a kindergarten teacher's unit` TIMES (1 MINUS `share of a position worked` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a day in two weeks is 10% of the unit`

-- 3א: a coordinating teacher, mother of a child up to 14, whom her employer
-- requires to work a full position, gets a 10% mother supplement beyond the
-- position.
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12__para_3__subpara_a
GIVEN m IS A `mother kindergarten teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `mother supplement beyond the position` m IS
    IF m's `a coordinating teacher required by her employer to work a full position` AND m's `mother of a child up to 14`
    THEN 0.1
    ELSE 0

-- 3ב: a teacher entitled to age hours who is a mother of a child up to 14
-- has her position base reduced and gets the mother supplement "as
-- required". The size of the reduction is the age-hours rule's (1.23).
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12__para_3__subpara_b akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12__para_3__subpara_b/p2
GIVEN m IS A `mother kindergarten teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `base reduced and mother supplement too` m IF
    m's `entitled to age hours` AND m's `mother of a child up to 14`

@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12__para_3__subpara_c
GIVEN `entitled to a training day under the old rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeps the training day` `entitled to a training day under the old rules` IF
    `entitled to a training day under the old rules`

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12/p2 A source: collective agreement of 15.5.89; director-general's circular שן/3.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12/p3 A source: agreement with the Teachers' Union of 15.7.91.
-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12/p4 A heading ("age hours").

-- Age hours: the rules for an elementary-school teacher apply (section 1.23).
@ref akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12/p5
ASSUME `the age-hours rules of section 1.23` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER

-- akn:chp_2__sec_2_1__ssec_2_1_12/p6 A pointer to section 1.23, age hours for teachers and kindergarten teachers.

-- Worked examples; the salary of 9,000 is a placeholder.
#ASSERT `hourly pay of a teacher's substitute` 9000 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `weekly hours in a kindergarten teacher's unit` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `earliest end of the day` Purim FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 690
#ASSERT `earliest end of the day` Hanukkah TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 660
#ASSERT `daily compensation for being alone` TRUE 2 50 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the assistant watches the children until` 800 600 640 EQUALS 600

`a 19-year-old candidate` MEANS
    `assistant's substitute` WITH
        `age`                                    IS 19
        `clean and tidy appearance`              IS TRUE
        `inclined to work with children`         IS TRUE
        `responsible at work`                    IS TRUE
        `elementary knowledge of child care`     IS TRUE
        `reads and writes Hebrew at elementary-school level` IS TRUE
        `can keep an orderly household`          IS TRUE
#ASSERT `qualified to substitute for an assistant` `a 19-year-old candidate`

#TRACE `sending by priority` (LIST `an unplaced teacher`, `a kindergarten-teachers' seminar student`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person responsible for substitutions` DOES `send a substitute` `an unplaced teacher` AT 10
#TRACE `sending by priority` (LIST `an unplaced teacher`, `a kindergarten-teachers' seminar student`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person responsible for substitutions` DOES `send a substitute` `a kindergarten-teachers' seminar student` AT 10
#TRACE `claiming the compensation` 50 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the kindergarten assistant` DOES `claim the payment for being alone` TRUE AT 1
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the assistant's daily compensation` 50 AT 2
